  "faithful": "Cornay—Considerable diversity of weights and measures is found in the various states into which this extensive coun-try is divided, and the most important of them will be found instantly. But now a few of their standards, though differing in amount, are similar in their multiples and subdivisions. the weights, 1024 hellers = 312 pfennings = 128 quintins = 16 ounces = 2 marks = 12 oz. = 1 apothecaries' lb.; and 5700 grains = 288 scruples = 96 drachms = 12 oz. = 1 apothecaries' lb.; 4352 eschen = 512 hellers = 256 pfennings = 64 quintins = 16 lots = 8 oz. = 1 Cologne mark = 3608 grains troy. By this d and silver are weighed; and the fineness of gold is expressed 24 parts or carats as in Britain, but the fineness of silver by 16 parts. For jewellery there is a carat of 3-171 grs. troy. Of measures, 144 inches = 12 feet = 6 ells = 2 klafter = 4 ruthe. the Rhinland foot used by surveyors = 12-36 Brit. inches; the mile = 10,126 Brit. yds., the short mile = 6859, and the geographical mile = 8101 Brit. yds. The Rhinland morgen of 10 = 10,185 Brit. sq. yds.",
